2 CONT
2 CONT "Louis De Rees, född omkr 1500 i Bryssel, Belgien; † där 1555-10-23. Blev 1531-09-01 jämte sina bröder adlad av kejsaren Karl V. Gift 1526-08-07 i Bryssel, Belgien med Margaretha (de Ruis) Derris, född omkr 1505 i Amtrup, Nederlän
2 CONC derna, † 1556-02-04 i Bryssel, dotter till Peter Derris."
2 CONT
2 CONT Margareta de Rees Derris was born around 1505 in Amtrup, Netherlands, and she passed away on February 4, 1556, in Brussels, Belgium. She was the daughter of Peter Derris. Margareta married Louis De Rees, who was adladed by Emperor
2 CONC  Charles V along with his brothers in 1531. Their son, Thomas De Rees, was born in 1535 and became a merchant. Thomas later fled to Hamburg, Germany, due to his religious beliefs and fear of the Spanish Inquisition. He married Cla
2 CONC ra Gillesdotter de Greve, and they had 11 children
