1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Wrangel_af_Sage_och_Waschel_nr_1850 '''Otto Reinhold Wrangel, till Sage''']. Löjtnant i svensk tjänst. Manngerichtsassessor i Wierland. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Död före 1663''' juli. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Gift 1:o 1653''' med '''Barbara Maria von Klebeck''', dotter av lantrådet och ståthållaren på Kokenhusen Henrik von Klebeck och Margareta von Löwenwolde. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Gift 2:o 1658''' med '''Dorotea Elisabet von Lode''', dotter av mannrichtern Rötgert von Lode och Hedvig von Fersen.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Wrangeli Interpretation of Wrangeli Counts, Barons and Nobles of Danish Descent. Information about this ancient genus reaches the beginning of the XII century. The ancestor of the family V. belonged to the number of vassals of Kin
2 CONC g Valdemar II, left by him in Estonia, after the first conquest of it. In the castle 'Revele' (later the city of Revel) a Danish garrison was placed in 1219, at the head of which was a certain number of 'husbands of the king' (vir
2 CONC i regis) and between them there is Dominus Tuki Wrang, whose descendants were first called de Wranghele, Wrangele, And then B. During the Swedish rule in Estland in the 17th century, the V. family achieved splendor and wealth in t
2 CONC he person of Field Marshal Karl Gustav. Then the members of this genus become so numerous that it gradually loses its significance. Most of all, Wrangels advanced in the military field, in the service not only of Denmark and Swede
2 CONC n, but also of Germany, Austria, Holland and Spain, and subsequently Russia. They gave 7 field marshals, more than 30 generals, 7 admirals; Some of them were elevated for their services to the dignity of counts (in Sweden, Spain, 
2 CONC Germany); In 1709, after the battle near Poltava, on the battlefield, 22 representatives of the B clan remained on the Russian service only in the last period of the Seven Years War and in subsequent Turkish wars. Of these, there 
2 CONC were 18 generals, 2 admirals. Among the representatives of the clan V. in the civil and spiritual arenas can be noted: Swedish bishops (Dorpat 1400 and Revel 1658), 4 abbess, 7 envoys, 11 members of the state council and 1 ministe
2 CONC r; In Russia: in the positions of minister - 1, member of the state council - 1, senators - 2, governors - 2, trustee of an educational district - 1, professor - 1. In the 16th century, the V. family split into 20 independent line
2 CONC s. At present, in terms of their number, representatives of the Russian lines of the genus V. occupy the first place (40), the Swedish ones - the second (37), the Prussian - the third (11). K. V.
2 CONT
