1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Nils Gyllenstierna af Fogelvik=
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nils_Gyllenstierna '''Nils Carlsson Gyllenstierna af Fogelvik'''], a member of the Swedish baronial family of [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gyldenstierne_(noble_family%29 '''Gyllenstierna'''], was a
2 CONC  Swedish field-marshal, member of the Royal Council, president of the Board of War, and governor-general of [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bremen-Verden '''Bremen-Verden''']. Rewarded with the earldom of [https://en.wikipedia.org/
2 CONC wiki/F%C3%A5gelvik_Manor '''Fågelvik'''], he belonged to the cautious senior officers, who he hesitated when faced with [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charles_XII_of_Sweden '''Charles XII''']'s aggressive plans, and allied with hi
2 CONC s son-in-law [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arvid_Horn '''Arvid Horn'''] in opposition to the King.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Early career===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Gyllenstierna studied at''' the universities of Rostock and Königsberg. At the outbreak of the Swedish war with Bremen in 1666, he enlisted as a pikeman in Swedish service, but was soon commissioned; reaching captain's rank in 
2 CONC 1668. Gyllenstierna undertook a grand tour 1669-1672, which also included a visit with the Knights of Malta. When the French in 1672 attacked the Dutch Republic, Gyllenstierna became captain in a regiment of the Prince-Bishopric o
2 CONC f Munster that fought against the Dutch, but soon became major in a regiment of the Prince-Bishopric of Osnabruck that was in Dutch service, and there promoted to lieutenant-colonel in 1674.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Senior officer===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''When the''' [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scanian_War '''Scanian war'''] began in 1675, Gyllenstierna was recalled by the Swedish government; becoming colonel of [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scanian_Hussar_Regiment '''Scania
2 CONC n Hussar Regiment'''] in 1677. In 1693 he was promoted to major-general of cavalry and appointed governor of Jönköping county; in 1696 to lieutenant-general, and governor of Swedish Wismar; and in 1698 to general of cavalry, and g
2 CONC overnor-general of Bremen-Verden. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''At the outbreak''' of the [https://www.geni.com/projects/The-Great-Northern-War-1700-1721/640960 '''Great Northern War'''], Gyllenstierna who was commander-in-chief of the Swedish forces in Germany, crossed the Elbe, and beat t
2 CONC he Danes at Reinbek. In 1702 he commanded the Swedish reinforcements that were transferred from Germany to Poland. In 1708, he commanded the forces of the Lower Saxon Circle that occupied Hamburg, and was rewarded for the successf
2 CONC ul operation with promotion to field-marshal. Although a royal councillor since 1705, Gyllenstierna remained in Germany until 1711, when he returned to Sweden, becoming president of the Board of War. Between 1714 and 1719 he was a
2 CONC lso commander-in-chief of the Swedish forces in Skåne.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Political role===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Gyllenstierna belonged''' to the cautious senior officers who hesitated before the aggressive plans of Charles XII. His objections lead to the shelving of a planned attack on the Electorate of Saxony in 1701; he also argued aga
2 CONC inst the invasion of the Polish–Lithuanian Commonwealth. After the battle of Poltava, Gyllenstierna opposed the rearmament policy advocated by [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Magnus_Stenbock '''Magnus Stenbock'''], as too onerous f
2 CONC or the country, and in the Royal Council he joined with his son-in-law Arvid Horn in his opposition to the absent King. In the power struggle after the death of the King, Gyllenstierna again allied with Horn, but died in 1720.
2 CONT
2 CONT /////
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Gyllenstierna_af_Fogelvik_nr_47 '''Nils Gyllenstierna af Lundholm''', ''greve'' '''Gyllenstierna af Fogelvik, till Fågelvik'''] i Tryserums socken, Kalmar län samt herre till Vittvik och Stjär
2 CONC neborg i [https://sv.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tryserums_socken '''Tryserums socken'''], samt Hällerö i Eds socken, (alla i Kalm.). 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Född 1648-10-13''' i [https://www.geni.com/projects/Hanseatic-Town-of-Wismar-Mecklenburg-West-Pomerania-Germany/4475629 '''Wismar''']. Student i Uppsala 1662 och i Rostock 1663, sedan i Königsberg. Pikenerare vid C. Gift Wrange
2 CONC ls livkompani i Bremen 1666. Fänrik vid Kalmar regemente 1667. Löjtnant vid greve Dohnas regemente. Kapten därst. 1668. Major vid Ulfsparres regemente i holländsk tjänst 1672. Överstelöjtnant därst. 1674. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Överstelöjtnant vid''' prästdragonerna i Sverige 1676. Överste för ett regemente till häst, som han själv uppsatte 1677. Överste för norra skånska kavalleriregementet 1679. Generalmajor av kavalleriet och landshövding i Jönköpi
2 CONC ngs län 1693. Generallöjtnant, guvernör i Wismar samt överste för garnisonsregementet därst. 1696. Kallades 1697 till lantmarskalk, men hindrades därifrån av åkommen sjukdom. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''General av kavalleriet''', generalguvernör över Bremen och Verden samt överste för garnisonsregementet i Stade 1698. Befälhavare över alla svenska trupper i Tyskland 1699. K. råd 1705. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Greve 1706-07-20''' (20/6) (introd. 1719 under n:o 47). 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Fältmarskalk 1709'''. President i krigskollegium 1710. Överbefälhavare över trupperna i Skåne 1714. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Död 1720-03-30''' och slöt själv på svärdssidan sin grevl. att samt begraven s. å. 7/4, i konung Fredriks närvaro, i Kungsholms kyrka i Stockholm. 
2 CONT
2 CONT  "Han var en mycket begagnad och driftig ämbetsman. Såsom, befälhavare över trupperna i Tyskland övergick han efter danska krigets utbrott 1700 Elbe med 10,000 man och slog danskarna vid Reinbeck. 1702 tillförde han konung Carl XI
2 CONC I i Polen en förstärkning av 12,000 man och 1708 besatte han med nedersachsiska kretsens trupper staden Hamburg i anledning av inre oroligheter därst. Såsom den äldsta av rådet bar han kronan vid konung Carl XILs begravning och, j
2 CONC ämte ärkebiskopen påsatte henne vid drottning Ulrika Eleonoras kröning." 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Gift 1680-07-21''' i Stockholm med sin sysslings dotter, grevinnan [https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Gyllenstierna_af_Bj%C3%B6rksund_och_Helg%C3%B6_nr_45 Anna '''Christina Gyllenstierna af Björksund och Helgö'''], född 1657
2 CONC -11-13 på [https://sv.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bj%C3%B6rksund Björksund], död 1715-08-25 i Stockholm och begraven s. å. 29/8 i Kungsholms kyrka, dotter av riksrådet och presidenten, friherre Göran Gyllenstierna af Lundholm, greve Gyllen
2 CONC stierna av Björksund och Helgö, och Barbro Margareta Banér.
2 CONT
2 CONT /////
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.nad.riksarkivet.se/sbl/Presentation.aspx?id=13415
