2 CONT =History =
2 CONT
2 CONT Carl was born at Femsjö parish and the place where Elmhult. Femsjö is located in the southwest part of Småland along the border of Halland. The father was Bengt Andersson and modern Christina Rosenschantz. When church records in F
2 CONC emsjö from this time are well conducted, it became as a highway back in time.Carl's grandfather born in Denmark let us go back to 1644 on May 26 at the Koldingshus Castle in Jutland. Then was born Johan Carl, who would become the 
2 CONC father of Carl's mother, Christina Rosenschantz. The father of Johan Carl was future Commandant and Länshövding in Landskrona County, Jörgen Gÿnter. The mother's name was Brigitta Wolff Jörgen Gÿnter began as a private soldier in 
2 CONC the wars of Gustavus Adolphus and advanced over the years to the Colonel with his own Regiment.He was knighted on 14 July 1652, and then took the name Rosenschantz.
2 CONT
2 CONT Johan Carl Rosenschantz was born during the so-called Torstensson war when the Swedes during the thirty years ' war made a detour and invaded Denmark from the South. You could say he was born to a soldier, for already in 1649 and 
2 CONC 1650 years rolls (5-6 years old?!), he is listed as a second lieutenant in his father's company.1660, he was wounded at Västerbottens regemente, where his father was Gynter Rosenschantz
2 CONT
2 CONT Regimental Commander. After his mother's death in September 1659, and the death of his father on 31 March 1662, Johan Carl was left alone with their underage siblings. In a letter to the King, he wants to get the money that his fa
2 CONC ther had in outstanding wages of 1662, to give his father a decent burial. Some money from the Regency, it becomes not as evidenced by a letter later in the article. Self-sufficient person in Landskrona, Sweden during the time of 
2 CONC the funeral, he gets the help of Per Hammarsköld (Governor-elect), who in a letter to the Governor general requesting that Johan Carl get his salary for the month of May and allowances for subsistence. Johan Carl is faithfully Väs
2 CONC terbotten Regiment until 3 August 1675, when he received the Royal power of Attorney being Lieutenant under Lieutenant Colonel von Rappolts Squadron and Salt Peter's Jews. He rose to the rank of Captain and finished his military c
2 CONC areer as regementsväbel
2 CONT
2 CONT Johan Carl marries Maria Chatarina Svinhuvfud August 21 1666, in Mulseryd, located in the northern part of Småland. The timing corresponds well with the gift of 18 mark appearing in Mulseryds kyrkobok as a gift of the right J C Ro
2 CONC senschantz.  After the wedding, the couple settled on the farm Haque in Laxarby parish in Dalsland and älvsborg County, which is confirmed in 1668 where Laxarbys kyrkobok "Wälborne Rosenschantz paid the 1 d 4 Penny" in church tax.
2 CONC  Here is probably their first child was born after 1668, there will be a gap until 1677. When the family showed up in Femsjö in small country and at seat farm Yaböke.Yaböke and Gullnubb farm cottage was a donation to Johan Carl's 
2 CONC wife Maria Catharina Svinhufvud grandfather Per Jonsson on 9 November, 1624 by King Gustav II Adolf. Ownership can also be gleaned by the register of the lengths.Yaböke seat located on farm Road North seen from Femsjö Church. In F
2 CONC emsjö Herdaminne says the following to read: "1681.
2 CONT
2 CONT The parish priest complained for neglect religious services, rejects the communicants, because they didn't make  their communion day labor, taken for high likstod, m.m. Complaints were raised by a poor nobleman, J C Rosenschantz, 
2 CONC that for manslaughter he has been denied the sacrament. At an inspection in July of the same year, requested the Assembly to be vicar RID, since it's considerable annoyance. Among other things, he had allowed the work to be perfor
2 CONC med on the last big böndag, both before and after the service. The congregation was admonished to conciliation with the priest, for their offences had been suspended for half a year. If the priest Bononius would of told them that 
2 CONC during the war, they must hold the worship service at Avjeberget, on the road to London ". Maybe it was for the aforementioned manslaughter, but it may also be due to Karl XI reduction, which Johan Carol became required by the Got
2 CONC a Court of Appeal to pay 195 daler sm. In a letter to the National Count, Mangus Gabriel de la Gardie, he wrote the following: "Högborne Count Canseler of the Kingdom of Sweden, and T Nådige Lord and Mächtige facilitators. Esther 
